WineD3D island: record the draw-state indirect-call base used by p66--p69.

The p66 native DRAW experiment exposed four callback families that patch 63 did
not yet record: shader backend, vertex pipe, fragment pipe, and state apply
(including the multistate arrays). Route all of them through the existing
fail-closed class A/B/C dispatcher as sites 32--35.

The separable-shader cache was the second exposed boundary defect. Native ARM
must not cache a guest x86 pointer returned by wglGetProcAddress(); resolve it
through the translated native GL table instead. NULL preserves the established
monolithic-program fallback.

This patch is an incremental source-of-record prerequisite for p69. It records
code already exercised by p66/p67/p68; it makes no new correctness or frame-rate
claim by itself.

